TIKI
setup
{
	scale 0.52
	path models/items/healthpacks
	skelmodel healthcanteen.skd
	surface material1 shader healthcanteen
}

init
{
	server
	{
		classname Health
		amount 25
		dmamount 25
		pickupsound med_canteen
	}
}

animations
{
	idle healthcanteen.skc
}

/*QUAKED item_health_25 (0 0 0) (0 0 0) (0 0 0)
Gives 25 Health when picked up.
Alias TIK placed at models/item_health_25.tik so the bare classname
lookup from the m6l1c BSP entity (targetname t1420, "item" "item_health_25"
on the ai_german_Wehrmacht_officer) resolves to a valid Health entity.
The exec coop_mod/itemhandler.scr line was intentionally omitted: this
item is given to an actor's inventory (not placed in the world), so the
world-item initialisation thread must not run on it.
*/
